    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u compare the efficiency of signalized intersections vs roundabouts for a high-volume urban junction? looking for info on throughput and how they handle peak hour friction/delays.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For high-volume urban junctions, roundabouts typically offer superior throughput and significantly lower delays during peak hours compared to traditional signalized intersections. While signals allow for precise control, they often create extended queues and stop-and-go friction at critical choke points, whereas roundabouts operate as queuing systems without individual vehicle stops, smoothing traffic flow even during surges. Consequently, roundabouts generally reduce total trip time by 15–20% and lower crash rates by eliminating turning lanes and red light黃灯 confusion. However, they do require more right-of-way utilization and careful geometric design to prevent bottlenecks under extreme congestion levels.",
